        "thinking": "`readFileSync` throws an error: `new Error(\"node:fs.readFileSync not available in CF Workers\")`.\n\nIn `readStore()` and `readSettings()`, these use `try { ... } catch { return default_value }`. So when `readFileSync` throws, the catch block returns the default value (`[]` or `{ disabledTypes: [] }`). \n\nThis means importing `registry.ts` in CF will:\n1. Register built-in adapters (via `registerBuiltInAdapters()`) - this works fine\n2. IIFE starts: calls `buildExternalAdapters()` → `listAdapterPlugins()` → `readStore()` → `readFileSync` throws → catch returns `[]` → no external adapters loaded\n\n\n3. IIFE completes with no external adapters loaded\n\nWhen `listServerAdapters()` runs, it returns all 10 built-in adapters. For `buildAdapterInfo`, the disabled types check fails gracefully and returns an empty list, so all adapters show as enabled with `source: \"builtin\"` and no version information since there's no external adapter record to read from disk.\n\nNow I need to check whether `isOverridePaused` also relies on filesystem operations.",
